Deployment Models: Public, Private, Hybrid, Community.
	Public Cloud: In Public cloud,the shared access to computing services are given to the users that is, users can share the same infrastructure for their applications.
	Private Cloud: Private cloud is a pool of resources meant exclusively for a single organization. It can either be owned by an organization or can be rented from a cloud provider.
	Hybrid cloud: Hybrid cloud refers to a cloud computing environment that uses the combination of both: the private cloud and the public cloud.
What is Microsoft Azure?
	Microsoft Azure is a cloud provider owned by Microsoft; it provides various web-scale cloud services such as compute, storage, networking etc..
	Establishment: launched on February 1, 2010.
	Widely recognized: Used by more than 90% of Fortune 500 companies
	Cost effective: Free to get started; offers the pay-per-use pricing model
	Multi-language support: Supports multiple languages viz. c#, NodeJS, Java and more
	Availability Zones: Data centers in 54 regions around the world, and available in 140 countries..(datacenters.microsoft.com/globe/explore)



Data centers:
A data center is a physical facility or building that houses computer systems, servers, and related equipment to store, process, and manage digital data

Availability zones:
An availability zone (AZ) is a physically separate, isolated fault domain within a cloud region that contains one or more discrete data centers with independent power, cooling, and networking

Regions:
A cloud region is a specific, independent geographic area where a cloud provider houses physical data centers


